From 76b1562890024726178d046f6f7a23535a256bfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:49:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: surround as Dolby asks the output, as Kodi's
 transcode does

"Surround as Dolby when the display takes only stereo PCM" chose Dolby
Digital Plus from the audio data of the display and the E-AC-3
passthrough setting alone. Kodi's own transcode also asks the sink
whether the passthrough output takes it (CActiveAESink::SupportsFormat()
with RAW E-AC-3 at 48 kHz, 2.0), and for E-AC-3 that means 192 kHz on
the output, since it is packed at four times its rate. The HDA HDMI
codec limits the rates of an output to those of its display: a TV that
declares PCM up to 48 kHz and Dolby Digital Plus has an output without
192 kHz, the sink would not open for E-AC-3, and the engine would retry
it with no sound where Kodi would have chosen Dolby Digital. Not seen:
the LG C5 declares PCM up to 192 kHz; found by a review.

Each format is now taken only where the passthrough output takes it as
the transcode sends it (AE::PCM::StereoDisplayCase::eac3OutputTakes,
ac3OutputTakes, asked in DolbyForDisplay()): Dolby Digital Plus, else
Dolby Digital, else stereo PCM as before, with the reason in the log
("its output takes neither ..."; the line of a choice of Dolby Digital
says when Dolby Digital Plus was left out for the output). The help of
the setting says it, in the four languages.

Host test (TestAEPcmChannels): an output without E-AC-3 gives AC-3, one
with neither gives stereo, one with E-AC-3 only for a display of E-AC-3
only gives E-AC-3, and a display without Dolby still says so first;
the code before (the output not asked) and two more mutations fail it.
